# Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0)

<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/>

The working papers and briefs in this directory (`RTR-WP-*.pdf`, `RTR-BR-*.pdf`)
are released under CC BY-NC 4.0. The MIT licence at the repository root covers
the site code; these research outputs are covered here instead.

You are free to share and adapt these papers — quote them, extend them,
translate them, correct them, build them into other people's work — provided you
give appropriate credit to The Right to Read Campaign, link to the licence, and
indicate if changes were made.

The one restriction is commercial use. Derivative and scholarly reuse is the
point; others will have better ideas, and this licence is meant to let them act
on those ideas without asking permission. What it does not permit is selling
this work, or building a commercial product on top of it, without a separate
agreement.

Derived datasets and charts published by the Campaign are also CC BY-NC 4.0.
Analysis code deposited on Zenodo is MIT — Creative Commons licences are not
suitable for software.

For the underlying facts, cite the primary sources named in each paper, not this
repository.
